# NYSE_CALENDAR_COVERS_FROM = 2016-01-01 now, with 2016-2024 holidays/early
# closes generated from exchange_calendars, and any date before 2016-01-01
# now raises TradingCalendarPrecedesCoverageError instead of silently
# answering wrong. krepis-PR207 (litellm INFO log suppression) and
# krepis-PR208 (PyPI propagation budget) are later releases in this line.
krepis>=0.59.53
# portfolio_optimizer (PR 1 of portfolio-optimizer-260511 arc): cvxpy solves the
# constrained mean-variance program (MVO + L1 turnover + SOC vol-target);
# scikit-learn provides Ledoit-Wolf covariance shrinkage. Both are optional at
# import time — executor/portfolio_optimizer.py raises a clear ImportError if
# missing, so the legacy 1/n sizing path runs unaffected on environments that
# haven't pulled these in yet.
# cvxpy: the rest of this stack (arcticdb~=6.23, pyarrow~=25.0, pandas~=3.0)
# already resolves numpy to the 2.x series today — arcticdb 6.18.x and
# pyarrow 25.0.x both support numpy 2 (verified via PyPI metadata + a real
# `pip install -r requirements.txt`, numpy resolved to 2.4.6 even under the
# old <1.8 ceiling). cvxpy was the lone holdout: cvxpy>=1.8.0 declares
# `numpy>=2.0.0` in its own metadata (it imports numpy.lib.array_utils,
# which does not exist before numpy 2.0), so the old <1.8 ceiling here was
# never actually "for numpy<3 compatibility" as previously stated — numpy
# was already resolving to 2.x regardless of cvxpy's version. The real
# constraint cvxpy<1.8 enforced was just "don't hard-require numpy>=2.0.0
# at cvxpy's own import time," resting on an unverified (and false)
# assumption that numpy needed to stay <2 elsewhere in this graph. Range
# below matches what dependabot proposed in crucible-executor#388 (closed
# via `@dependabot ignore this dependency` pending this migration) so
# re-enabling dependabot afterward should not immediately re-propose a
# conflicting bump.
#
# scikit-learn pin stays upper-bounded pending separate verification of the
# 1.10 series; unrelated to the cvxpy/numpy coupling above.
cvxpy>=1.9.2,<1.10
scikit-learn>=1.9.0,<1.10
